From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:28:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] tcp-service-name: propagate the server's service.name
 in a TCP option

Upstream OBI cannot tell a client which service it is calling: the downstream
service.name is configured only on the downstream process. This patch has the
server write its own service.name (at most 25 bytes) into a TCP option (kind
26) on its response segments, once per connection; the client side reads it
and records it as the span's PeerServiceName. Patch 03 exports it as
peer.service.name on client spans and RED metrics.

Configuration: a new context_propagation value, tcp_service_name (bit 1<<2,
also part of "all"), independent of upstream's tcp. tcp keeps its upstream
meaning (trace context in kind 25 on requests); tcp_service_name alone sends
no trace context at all: the sk_msg path only fills msg_buffers for client
sockets and never creates or writes a traceparent.

VPC scope: by default the name is exchanged only with peers inside the host's
VPC. At load time the tpinjector fills the svc_name_peer_cidrs LPM trie with
the VPC IPv4/IPv6 CIDR blocks of every interface from EC2 instance metadata
(IMDSv2), or the private ranges (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 100.64/10,
fc00::/7) when there is no instance metadata (non-AWS hosts, IMDS disabled),
plus the networks of the host's interfaces (container bridges) and loopback.
A server only marks a passive socket as a responder, and a client only parses
kind 26, when the peer address is in the trie. ebpf.tcp_service_name_outside_vpc
(OTEL_EBPF_BPF_TCP_SERVICE_NAME_OUTSIDE_VPC) opts out and allows any peer.
The scope applies to tcp_service_name only; upstream tcp is unchanged.

Mechanism (tpinjector, sockops + sk_msg):
- svc_name_by_pid: service.name per instrumented server PID.
- sk_svc_name_map: name staged per server socket, emitted by the sockops
  header-option callbacks.
- svc_peer_name_map: name parsed from response segments, keyed by the sorted
  connection tuple; read by the generic (http_info_t) and Go
  (http_request_trace_t) tracers when the client request completes.

Server-response capture fix: a passive socket placed in sock_dir sends through
the sk_psock path, so tcp_sendmsg does not fire for its responses. The sk_msg
program therefore pulls the message data and fills msg_buffers on the server
path too, so the backup kprobe still captures plaintext HTTP/1 responses.
Without it, non-Go (kprobe-traced) servers lose every server span.

Renames after instrumentation: AllowPID runs in the discovery pipeline before
the Kubernetes / Docker process-event decorators (pkg/internal/appolly), so the
first svc_name_by_pid entry of a pod holds its pre-Kubernetes name. The
tpinjector registers exec.FileInfo.OnServiceNameChange per PID and re-records
the entry whenever SetUID / SetAutoServiceName changes the name; a name that
cannot be propagated (empty, > 25 bytes) deletes the entry instead of leaving a
stale one.

Only the TCP option is added; L7 payloads and headers are never modified.
Requires CAP_NET_ADMIN (cgroup sockops/sk_msg).

Source (fork wangzlei/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation): f1a30ef2 (TCP
service-name part only), f876ca4d, 0e69fbc0, 221648bd. The request-head AWS SDK
parser that f1a30ef2 also carried is intentionally not included: AWS calls are
handled by upstream payload extraction instead.

Adot-Obi-Patch: 01-tcp-service-name
